simcyto provenance and redistribution record
============================================

This package contains reusable simulation machinery that was derived from
simulation code used in the FAUST benchmarking manuscript workflow. The public
upstream source identified in the `RGLab/faust_manuscript_analyses` repository is
`faustRuns/simulation/functionsForBenchmarking.R` (ref
`f86f1ab19a41fd2690bf180a7dcf483f9552950c`), as used by the FAUST
benchmarking framework. The repository, file path and upstream ref are recorded
here.

Upstream-Repository: RGLab/faust_manuscript_analyses
Upstream-File: faustRuns/simulation/functionsForBenchmarking.R
Upstream-Ref: f86f1ab19a41fd2690bf180a7dcf483f9552950c

The adapted code in `simcyto` is restricted to the reusable simulation engine
and intentionally excludes the downstream statistical-evaluation, mixed-model,
and benchmarking logic from the upstream manuscript-analysis repository.

Registered provenance for migrated components
--------------------------------------------

- Scenario builders and simulation hierarchy
  - Source: public upstream `faustRuns/simulation/functionsForBenchmarking.R` in
    `RGLab/faust_manuscript_analyses` (ref
    `f86f1ab19a41fd2690bf180a7dcf483f9552950c`); the local downstream
    `functionsForBenchmarking-Pheno.R` is the project-local adapted variant.
  - Adapted into: `simCytBuildScenario()`, `simCytScenarioUnivariate()`,
    `simCytScenarioBivariate()`, `simCytExperiment()`, `simCytSample()`,
    `simCytCondition()`, and `simCytCluster()`

- Distributional and cluster simulation logic
  - Source: public upstream `faustRuns/simulation/functionsForBenchmarking.R` in
    `RGLab/faust_manuscript_analyses` (ref
    `f86f1ab19a41fd2690bf180a7dcf483f9552950c`); the local downstream
    `functionsForBenchmarking-Pheno.R` is the project-local adapted variant.
  - Adapted into: `simCytClusterData()`, `simCytCluster()`

- Positive-definite covariance generation helper
  - Source: the commonly cited R-help / R programming community approach for
    generating random positive-definite matrices, credited to Ravi Varadhan
  - Adapted into: `.posDef()` in `R/cov_helpers.R`
  - This helper is a small, self-contained numerical routine and is treated as a
    nested third-party provenance item rather than as a separate software
    component with its own licensing baggage.

- Ratio correction and perturbation machinery
  - Source: public upstream `faustRuns/simulation/functionsForBenchmarking.R` in
    `RGLab/faust_manuscript_analyses` (ref
    `f86f1ab19a41fd2690bf180a7dcf483f9552950c`); the local downstream
    `functionsForBenchmarking-Pheno.R` is the project-local adapted variant.
  - Adapted into: the perturbation and ratio-correction helpers used by
    `simCytExperiment()` and related simulation routines

Redistribution basis
--------------------

The package is distributed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or
later (`GPL (>= 3)`) as recorded in `DESCRIPTION`. The FAUST package itself is
GPL-compatible. The reused manuscript-analysis code is treated as a GPL-
compatible source for the simulation engine only, and the package does not
retain any downstream benchmark-analysis code that was not independently
reviewed for redistribution suitability.

This record is intended to provide the authoritative provenance statement for
this codebase and to document the provenance chain before release. If upstream
maintainers provide a more specific licensing or attribution clarification, this
record should be updated to reflect that position.
